    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17514902/005056a3-d347-1fe1-acda-b2ade16d82be": {
      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, NURSING - SCHOOL OF HEALTH SCIENCES Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 04 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer, Nursing in the School of Health Sciences. The position is full-time. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Palliative Care Nursing Peri-operative Nursing Medical-Surgical Nursing Community Health Nursing Paediatric Nursing Geriatric Nursing Mental Health Nursing Nursing Research Integrated Nursing Science Pharmacology 2. Implement the latest ICT-enabled learning pedagogies and support the development of these tools. 3. Provide pastoral care to students to support learning. 4. Support school’s outreach efforts, students’ local and overseas programmes. 5. Support academic support duties and any other duties as assigned. What we are looking for A degree in nursing. At least 3 years’ working experience in clinical and/or hospital setting in Singapore. Familiar with clinical practice at hospital wards and the teaching of the inter-relationship between normal body functioning and the underlying physiology, pathophysiological mechanism of diseases states and their pharmacological management is essential. Proficient in Microsoft Word and Excel. Additional pre-requisites that are advantageous: Post- Graduate Diploma in Higher Education, Advanced Certificate in Training and Assessment (ACTA) and/or Diploma in Adult Continuing Education (DACE). About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCH OF INFOCOMM TECHNOLOGY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 27 Sep 2026 LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 27 Sep 2026 LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 27 Sep 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 27 Sep 2026 LECTURER - ACCOUNTANCY, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 04 Oct 2026 [LTA-QSC2] MGR/DEPUTY/ASSISTANT MGR, STRATEGIC ENGAGEMENT & COLLABORAT Land Transport Authority Closing on 01 Oct 2026 Senior Executive - Examinations Development  [ITE Headquarters] – 1 Yr Institute Of Technical Education Closing in 1  day(s) Adjunct Lecturer (Veterinary Technology / Veterinary Wellness Care) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 LECTURER, NURSING - SCHOOL OF HEALTH SCIENCES Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 04 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17713880/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-adbf-433294b3740b": {
      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, AI & DIGITAL TRANSFORMATION - SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 04 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer, Artificial Intelligence & Digital Transformation in the School of Business & Accountancy. What you will be working on As a Lecturer, you will: Develop and deliver curriculum (including online courses) and assessments for full-time and part-time courses for students and adult learners. Supervise student projects and internships with industry partners. Counsel and mentor students to support their learning and personal development, provide education and career guidance, and coach them for competitions. Undertake academic-related administration and committee work, support outreach activities and study trips, and ad-hoc projects that support the school’s mission. Plan, lead, manage and develop industry projects. What we are looking for At least 3 years of relevant industry experience; teaching or training experience is a plus. Relevant industry certifications or professional qualifications in AI, analytics, digitalisation, business transformation, and/ or adult learning are a bonus. Training and Adult Educator Professional Pathway (TAEPP) registered. Interested and confident in teaching artificial intelligence, data analytics, digital transformation, business innovation, Generative AI, and related topics in both PET and CET programmes. Experienced professionally in business application of AI, analytics and machine learning. Knowledge and experience in AI-driven workforce transformation, data visualisation tools, and automation will be an added advantage. A passionate educator with a nurturing mindset and strong rapport with students. A team player with strong presentation and communication skills. Creative in using digital tools and tech-enabled strategies to enhance student engagement. A team player who thrives in a dynamic environment and can manage multiple projects independently. Having access to industry partners/networks will be an advantage as you may be required to spearhead new development initiatives and industry collaborations. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER, NURSING - SCHOOL OF HEALTH SCIENCES Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 04 Oct 2026 LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCH OF INFOCOMM TECHNOLOGY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER - ACCOUNTANCY, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 04 Oct 2026 [TT26D] General Education Officer (with teaching qualifications) MOE- HQ Closing in 6  day(s) Office of Staff Development - Mgr/Snr Mgr (Talent & Leadership Devt) [ Republic Polytechnic Closing on 29 Sep 2026 LECTURER, AI & DIGITAL TRANSFORMATION - SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 04 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18077534/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-adbf-414a9c99540b": {
      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button AI ENGINEER - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 04 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position with the Digital Services & Technology Office. The AI Engineer will be instrumental in implementing NP's AI transformation strategy by developing production-ready AI applications and systems that leverage AI tools and Cloud AI services. This role focuses on building robust, scalable AI solutions using GenAI models, deep learning, neural networks, and other AI technologies to improve NP operations through intelligent automation and advanced analytics. Working in close collaboration with the AI Product Manager, data scientists, and cross-functional teams, the AI Engineer will transition AI models from research to production and embed AI capabilities into NP's administrative and academic support workflows. What you will be working on AI Solution Development Design, develop, and implement AI/ML models, algorithms, and GenAI-powered applications (including conversational AI, content generation, and intelligent document processing systems) using diverse approaches and platforms such as Microsoft Copilot Studio, Databricks Apps, Azure AI Studio, and custom development frameworks. Deploy and integrate AI solutions with existing enterprise systems, ensuring compatibility with data infrastructure and institutional workflows. Model Development & Operations Design, build, and train machine learning, deep learning, and neural network models tailored to address specific institutional needs across administrative and operational domains. Collect, analyse, and clean data from various sources to train and test AI models, working closely with data engineering teams to ensure data quality and accessibility. Test, validate, and optimise algorithms to ensure reliability, scalability, and performance across various use cases and production environments Technical Implementation Configure and utilise AI development environments and tools within the AI platform infrastructure provided by the infrastructure team. Implement MLOps practices including automated model training, testing, deployment pipelines, version control, and continuous integration for AI solutions. Deploy AI models and applications using cloud AI services (Azure, AWS) and platform infrastructure, ensuring optimal performance and resource utilisation. Develop APIs and microservices to serve AI models, enabling robust integration with institutional workflows and applications. Quality Assurance & Support Ensure AI solutions meet NP's technical standards for scalability, reliability, security, and maintainability while complying with data privacy regulations and ethical AI guidelines. Provide technical support, troubleshooting, and performance optimisation for deployed AI applications and models. Collaborate with Infrastructure team to define requirements for AI platform capabilities and provide feedback on platform performance and functionality. Work closely with data scientists, product teams, and business stakeholders to align AI solutions with institutional goals and embed AI capabilities into workflows. What we are looking for Degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Software Engineering, or a related technical discipline. Minimum 3 years of hands-on experience in AI/ML development with demonstrated expertise in building and managing both AI infrastructure and applications in production environments. Skills & Certifications Proficiency in programming languages such as Python, R, or Java, with experience in AI/ML frameworks like TensorFlow, PyTorch, scikit-learn, and related ecosystem tools. Experience with cloud platforms (Azure, AWS) including AI services, infrastructure-as-code, containerisation technologies (Docker, Kubernetes), and platform engineering practices. Expertise in MLOps tools and practices, including model lifecycle management, automated deployment pipelines, monitoring, and governance frameworks. Knowledge of data engineering concepts, API development, microservices architecture, and enterprise integration patterns. Experience with enterprise platforms such as Databricks, Microsoft Co-Pilot Studio, Power Platform, and familiarity with Singapore IT governance and security frameworks. Attributes Detail-focused and methodical. Problem-solver with a performance-driven mindset. Adaptable and collaborative within cross-functional teams. Strong communicator able to work across AI, governance, and business stakeholders. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in DATA & GOVERNANCE ARCHITECT - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) SENIOR PLATFORM & SECURITY ENGINEER - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OF Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) Assistant Director, Digital Synthesis Science Centre Board Closing on 15 Oct 2026 Robotics-AI Engineer Defence Science And Technology Agency Closing on 31 Oct 2026 Associate Cybersecurity Engineer (CSDP) July 2027 Intake MDDI-CSA Closing on 04 Apr 2027 Assistant Director (Digital) MINDEF DXO Closing on 17 Oct 2026 Manager (AI and Trust) Info-Communications Media Development Au Closing on 30 Dec 2026 GenAI Solutions Developer Intern MINDEF Closing on 18 Oct 2026 AI ENGINEER - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 04 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    }
